      "math_academy_id": "q-319385",
      "knowledge_point_id": "b194bf2f-feaa-5656-a3ee-0ff466a39e77",
      "knowledge_point": "Differentiating a Product Containing a Trigonometric Function",
      "problem": "Differentiate $\\sqrt{x}tan⁡(x).$\n\n$(\\sqrt{x}tan⁡(x))^{′}=\\frac{tan⁡(x)}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ and $v(x)=tan⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\sqrt{x}tan⁡(x))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{x})^{′}\\cdot tan⁡(x)+\\sqrt{x}\\cdot (tan⁡(x))^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}(tan⁡(x))+(\\sqrt{x})({sec}^{2}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{tan⁡(x)}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\sqrt{x}{sec}^{2}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\sqrt{x}\\sec(x)^2"
            }
          ],
          "correct_value": "\\sqrt{x}\\sec(x)^2"
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-319385",
        "kp_title": "Differentiating a Product Containing a Trigonometric Function",
        "kp_href": null
      }
    },
    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-104297",
